column5:
The river runs through the forest, trickling slowly.{w}
It'd be a downhill hike, due to Valinorth's location.{w}
I wonder where this stream would end up, though.{w}
In Valinorth, we redirected them all to the water tank.

column6:
河流穿过森林，缓缓流淌。{w}
由于瓦利诺斯的地势，这一路都是下坡。{w}
不过我倒想知道，这条溪流最终会流向哪里。{w}
在瓦利诺斯，我们把它们全都引流到蓄水池里。

column5:
The trees out here looked different than they did at home.{w}
Back in Valinorth, they were touched by civilization.{w}
Out here, they were untouched, and looked more wild.{w}
Even the scent in the air seemed a lot different.

column6:
这里的树木看起来和家乡的不一样。{w}
在瓦利诺斯，它们带着文明的痕迹。{w}
在这里，它们无人触碰，显得更加野性。{w}
连空气中的气味似乎都大不相同。

column5:
I tried looking as far back as I could.{w}
I thought I might be able to see where the stream led.{w}
But it went on too far, and I couldn't see a thing.{w}
It would be good to use as a landmark, so we don't get lost.

column6:
我试着尽量往远处看。{w}
我以为能看到溪流通向何处。{w}
但它延伸得太远，我什么也看不清。{w}
用它当路标应该不错，这样我们就不会迷路。

column5:
The ground is soft, and full of grass.{w}
It's growing out of control, I noticed right away.{w}
There was nobody out here to trim it like in the village.{w}
It's odd how so much can change due to an invisible line.

column6:
地面松软，长满了草。{w}
我一眼就注意到，它疯长得没人管。{w}
这里没人像村里那样修剪它。{w}
真奇怪，一条看不见的界线竟能带来这么多变化。

column5:
The leaves are swaying in the wind.{w}
A few fall down, and they soar around majestically.{w}
We're far enough from Eastcrown that they didn't wilt.{w}
It's amazing how much the spirits helped out our settlement.

column6:
树叶在风中摇曳。{w}
几片飘落下来，庄严地盘旋飞舞。{w}
我们离东冠足够远，所以它们没有枯萎。{w}
精灵对我们的聚居地帮助之大，真是不可思议。

column5:
As soon as we enter Sauleberg, we're all in shock.{w}
It's such a beautiful sight, unlike anything in Valinorth.{w}
From here, it's very obvious that we're up in the mountains.{w}
A fact that Valinorth's lush forests are prone to hide.

column6:
我们一进入索尔伯格，全都震惊了。{w}
那景色如此美丽，瓦利诺斯没有任何东西能与之相比。{w}
从这里看，很明显我们身处高山之上。{w}
这一点常被瓦利诺斯茂密的森林掩盖。
